function notes(){return `<div class="tiny-label">ON THIS PHONE · 4 NOTES</div><div class="card"><div class="meta">OCT 11 · FIELD NOTES</div><h3>The flood has a memory</h3><p>Town says the 1998 flood took 3 people. Archive says 4. One name was removed from every copy.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">OCT 13 · UNSENT</div><h3>Mara’s story changes</h3><p>She says she left before midnight. Jonah saw her car at the station at 2:17. One of them is lying—or one is remembering.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">OCT 14 · 1:52 AM</div><h3>Folder: AFTER THE WATER</h3><p>Hint: the gate only opens when the river lets go. October 14. Listen for the knock pattern.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">NO DATE · RECOVERED</div><h3>If I disappear</h3><p>Don’t trust a voice just because it remembers your name. The thing in the signal has all my memories. It is still not me.</p></div>`}
function files(){return `<div class="tiny-label">ELENA VOSS · LOCAL STORAGE</div><div class="file-row"><span>▤</span><span>Hollow Creek incident report.pdf</span><span class="file-lock">OPEN</span></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">INCIDENT REPORT · 1998 FLOOD</div><h3>Three residents recovered</h3><p>June Vale (17), Peter Ansel (42), Ruth Vale (39). Search called off October 15.</p><p style="color:#a75c4d">Handwritten correction: <b>FOUR</b>. Identity withheld at family request.</p></div><div class="file-row"><span>▧</span><span>dispatch_031.carbon</span><span class="file-lock">OPEN</span></div><div class="card"><div class="meta">NORTH STATION · DISPATCH CARBON</div><p>02:17 · Caller: E. Voss · Location: Old intake gate</p><p>Audio: 3 knocks. Pause. 1 knock. Caller says: <i>“I’m at the second step. Let me out.”</i></p></div><div class="file-row"><span>▣</span><span>AFTER THE WATER.enc</span><span class="file-lock">${state.unlocked?'UNLOCKED':'LOCKED'}</span></div>${state.unlocked?`<div class="ending"><div class="tiny-label">DECRYPTED · OCT 14 · 2:22 AM</div><p>There were four in the water. I was the one who came back.</p><p>At the gate I heard my own voice from below the second step. It knew my mother’s lullaby. It knew what Mara said when we were seventeen.</p><p>My mother died in that flood. Jonah erased the call because he heard me ask to be let out. But I was standing beside him.</p><p>If you have this phone, it found a way to send a message. The voice that asks you to open the last thread is not mine.</p><p><b>Do not answer. Do not come to the water.</b></p><p>— Elena</p><button class="action-btn" onclick="goHome();setTimeout(()=>openApp('unknown'),350)">Open the last thread</button></div>`:`<div class="card"><h3>Encrypted document</h3><p>Hint: the words scratched on the gate, together. One word. No spaces.</p><div class="password"><input id="pass" placeholder="ENTER PASSWORD" autocomplete="off" onkeydown="if(event.key==='Enter')checkPassword()"><button onclick="checkPassword()">DECRYPT</button></div><div class="result" id="pass-result"></div><p class="tiny-label">${state.clues.has('photo')?'CLUE FOUND · LOW TIDE':''}</p></div>`}`}
